{"step_index":3561,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T10:04:12Z","content":"That's exactly what's deployed. The [sovereign_orbs.html](file:///Users/ajoxendine68/Desktop/SSOT_Agentic_Brain/ops/scripts/fullscreen_ui/sovereign_orbs.html) engine is **pure raw WebGL** — zero Three.js, zero market libraries:\n\n**What's in the shaders (ours, hand-written):**\n- **Vertex shader**: Aspect-corrected quad positioning per orb\n- **Fragment shader**: Exponential glow falloff, white-hot core, particle dust ring with angular pulse, shimmer sparkle, activity-driven breathe animation\n- **Star field shader**: 600 point sprites with per-star brightness flicker\n- **Connection line shader**: Blended alpha lines between orb pairs, color-mixed from both agents\n\n**What drives the motion (our physics, no library):**\n- Spring-damped orbital mechanics — elastic snap to target orbit\n- Wobble harmonics — two-frequency organic float\n- Activity decay from real heartbeat timestamps — silence = dim + drift outward\n- Glow tracks `lastBeat` from `/api/quorum_activity`\n\n**Live now:**\n```\nhttp://127.0.0.1:8080/sovereign_orbs.html  →  HTTP 200\n```\n\nOpen it in Safari or Chrome. Three glowing orbs — cyan (Maxx), red-orange (Vance), green (Eden) — floating, breathing, connected by pulsing lines. No dependency on anything that isn't ours."}
